course: dictionary
lesson: 10499
title: One word, three meanings: twang
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word twang can be a sound, a way of speaking, or the action of making that sound. The words around it show you which meaning the writer means.
explain: «Maddie, with her new Aussie twang, can't follow a word.» Here a twang is part of how Maddie speaks. It is the accent in her voice, and it is so strong that other people cannot follow what she says.
explain: A string on a guitar, when plucked, makes a sharp, ringing sound: a twang. Think of a tight rubber band being pulled and let go. Two meanings are about sound, but one is about how people talk. Ask yourself: is this sound coming from a string, or from a voice?
fact: Twang can be a noun (a twang) or a verb (to twang).
fact: A twang is a sharp, ringing sound, like a tight string being plucked.
fact: A twang can also be a way of speaking where the voice sounds partly through the nose, as in «a Southern twang».
fact: To twang means to make that sound, or to pluck a string so it makes it.
fact: «An Australian twang» is one example of a twang in an accent, and it tells you where the speaker comes from.
exercise: In «Maddie, with her new Aussie twang, can't follow a word.» what does twang mean? | A sharp, ringing sound | To run very fast | A kind of warm hat | *A way of speaking, with the voice partly through the nose
exercise: Which word means a sharp, ringing sound like a plucked string? | Hush | Whisper | Splash | *Twang
exercise: Find and copy the word from «after a year she had a bit of an Aussie twang herself.» that names a way of speaking. | *twang | herself | year | bit
test: Which sentence uses twang as a verb, meaning to make a string sound? | Her twang was strong and clear | The twang of the guitar filled the room | The twangs were loud | *He twanged the guitar string so it rang out
test: Why might a character's voice have a twang? | It means they are lost | It shows they have a cold | *It shows where they come from | It makes them taller
exam: Which meaning of twang fits «Maddie, with her new Aussie twang, can't follow a word»? | *A way of speaking, part of an accent | A loud bang | A ringing sound made by a string | A rude word for a friend
